<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="JAS" style="id">- Bu New Testament</book>
  <para style="rem">Copy right</para>
  <para style="toc1">YAKUBU</para>
  <para style="toc2">YAKUBU</para>
  <para style="toc3">Yak</para>
  <para style="mt1">YAKUBU</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="JAS 1" />
  <para style="s">Shinniti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 1:1" />Tuˈmaˈ Yakubu, zheli ki Lya, nǝ mulban Yesu Almasihu, swamak gǝs kǝ kutl nǝ lopi ginǝ dlaˈga tǝn dǝp lǝɓa u. shinniˈ mulnalti.<verse eid="JAS 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="s">Laˈti mbadli nǝ Shindǝtl ga</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 1:2" />Yelsǝni ini, ǝn undiˈ bǝna kǝ shoti a mbi kini u aˈ pǝllin hwol tugi, <verse eid="JAS 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 1:3" />Kǝ manini cimbitl laˈti mbadlwakǝn u, nǝn ɗǝ zǝˈ ngashtibi. <verse eid="JAS 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 1:4" />Ikǝ ngashtibi nǝn njikǝˈ kyautǝn wasi, nǝn laˈti aˈ dǝm mul nalti nǝ ngaptiga, i laˈti bǝ kǝkǝn hwotl ullǝn wai. <verse eid="JAS 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 1:5" />In gonwakǝn a hwol maˈulǝn u, an ngyem Lya, mul bǝlti nǝ toh kǝ zoki , bǝnǝ laˈti biwai, Lya nǝn bǝtlti. <verse eid="JAS 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 1:6" />Amma an gyemi nǝ laˈti mbadli, bǝnǝ cetl mbadlwai, gaki mul cetl mbadli kǝnǝ lakumi kǝgeˈ balmal kǝn siɗa, ginǝ etǝl ɗǝ katti u, a ɗǝ jakǝnti <verse eid="JAS 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 1:7" />Bǝ undi mulu laˈmbadli tǝn mbiˈ ulǝn ama mulban wai. <verse eid="JAS 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 1:8" />Gaki timul mbatl lob kǝni, tiɗa zǝm mbatlwas nǝmmwai ageˈ lu mus kyautǝn waswai.<verse eid="JAS 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="s">Ulkǝtoh nǝ Bǝna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 1:9" />Mul shindǝtl ga tǝppǝ ɓulmǝn nǝ nal twasi. <verse eid="JAS 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 1:10" />mul usǝn tǝmpǝtl ɓulmǝn nǝshindǝtl gawasi, ama tǝm paˈti kǝnǝ buzhame. <verse eid="JAS 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 1:11" />In cin a celga nǝ mattwasu, me nǝn kokǝnti, a buzhewas lwaki a mbuntwas gǝli. nǝgu tǝmul usǝn gǝli geˈ dlom kǝ tǝleti nǝ palliti wasi.<verse eid="JAS 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s">Bǝna nǝ Cibǝlti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 1:12" />Albalka tǝn mul ngacciˈ cimbǝtl bi, inta ngash bi geˈ cimbǝltu, tǝn mbiˈ ul kǝndǝ ga kǝ Gu kǝ mbidli, gunǝ mulban pǝli miˈ lyapti ndǝtu. <verse eid="JAS 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 1:13" />In ka mbi cimbil tu, bǝˈ usu “Lya kǝn ɗǝ cimbitl ki wai.” Gaki Lya ɗa cimbitl mulǝn nǝ bezǝn lǝɓa wai, kǝn pǝti a cimbǝlǝn Lya nǝ bezǝn wai; <verse eid="JAS 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 1:14" />Amma in mulǝn ambi gawas geˈ cimbiltu lawaskǝn shelti, a tle gawasi. <verse eid="JAS 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 1:15" />Bezǝn lyap lǝɓa in apǝl tugu, nǝnzǝˈ byas lǝɓa. in byas lǝɓa analu nǝn mbǝtl mǝshti. <verse eid="JAS 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 1:16" />Bǝs gǝl kini waica, mil yelsǝni ini mudli nǝ mwani. <verse eid="JAS 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 1:17" />Mus mbuni bǝlti ki njǝˈni, sul lya kǝn ɗǝ peˈti, mul mbǝˈsum maˈ Mulban kǝ cilti, gunǝ bǝ ɗa shottwai u kǝnǝ gwasǝn mul shaˈti. <verse eid="JAS 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 1:18" />Iˈ oli tǝp bǝlǝn min zǝti tuˈma shilǝn ki bali, gaki tǝn dǝmni kǝnǝ nyoh ki kina kǝ mus halitta wasi<verse eid="JAS 1:18" /></para>
  <para style="s">Kub Shilǝn nǝ pǝlti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 1:19" />Mil yelsǝni ini mudli nǝ mwani, manǝngu: dleuwonkin ɗǝ gaˈti kǝm, bǝ dlewon kin ɗǝ shilǝn ko ɗǝ leutl mbadli wai, <verse eid="JAS 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 1:20" />gaki leukǝ mbatl ki yakǝn mbalǝn ɗa talaˈti ɗǝ pǝtl kyautǝn ki zoki ki Lya wai. <verse eid="JAS 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 1:21" />Gaki nǝgu, aˈ lakǝn mus kyautǝn ki bezǝn lǝɓa taka nǝ ngyem mbiti ki mbalǝn, shilǝn u nǝ dlilli geˈ mbadlwakǝn u, ndǝˈni nǝ nali geˈ shindǝtl ga, gaki tinǝ ndǝtl kǝ pekkǝtl dliwakǝn. <verse eid="JAS 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 1:22" />Dǝmni miˈ petl shilǝni, bǝmiˈ kumti katlwai, aki shatl gawakǝn wai. <verse eid="JAS 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 1:23" />gaki mus mulnǝ mul kup shilǝni katlu, bǝ mul pǝltiwai u, kǝnǝ mul nǝ ɗǝ yak kinawas age' boka u ni. <verse eid="JAS 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 1:24" />gaki tǝn yak kinawasi azzǝga, alǝbi alǝbi am musni nǝ tetwasi. <verse eid="JAS 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 1:25" />Amma mus mul nǝ ɗǝ yaˈ njikǝˈkǝ zhil ki mbiˈ ga u, inngash bi tǝnki u, tadǝm mul kumtikatl ammus niwai, addǝm mul pǝlti nǝ ɓotlti, gu sǝppǝliˈ albalka ageˈulnǝ ti pǝlti u. <verse eid="JAS 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 1:26" />In mulǝn ɗǝ patl gawasi ti mul bǝtl Lya kǝn u, amma bǝ ta ngab biwaswai u, iki bǝtl Lya wasu bali wai. <verse eid="JAS 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="JAS 1:27" />Bǝtl Lya ki zoki gunǝ bǝ bezǝn ulǝn ɗa giɓi wai u, akina ɗǝ Lya bwasinǝnˈ, iki kizi gulsi mudli, nǝˈ milu nǝ bǝ miˈ zǝssi ɗawai u, dwaɗǝn geˈ bǝna wasǝn u, aˈ pekkǝl gawaˈtaka ɗǝgeˈ bezǝn lǝɓa ki dǝp lǝɓa.<verse eid="JAS 1:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="JAS 2" />
  <para style="s">Matti tǝngeˈ elsǝni</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 2:1" />Yelsǝni ini mudli nǝ mwani, miˈ laˈti mbatl tǝn Yesu Almasihu mul nalti, bǝˈ shimǝn otl elsǝni geˈ mbadlwakǝn wai. <verse eid="JAS 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 2:2" />In mul ulkǝ shimi toh kǝ zinaliya nǝ luˈ lǝgǝl kǝ zokki a mbǝ geˈlu dobga wakǝn u, i mul nǝ bǝ ulǝn nidɗawai u a teteˈ kǝ dlili nǝ keci luˈlǝgǝlu. <verse eid="JAS 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 2:3" />In ka ngǝtlin nǝ natl mul laˈti zoˈ luˈlǝgǝlu, iˈ ulǝn tisu, “Kundǝn kǝngu kǝ zoki gawagi,” Amma iˈ ulǝn mul nǝ bǝ ulǝn nidɗawai usu, “dlil tyaka” ko “kuma dǝm atli a kina ɗaka,” <verse eid="JAS 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 2:4" />Ase bǝ otl elsǝni geˈ dlomwa kǝn nǝ dambǝtl kǝ ngashti ageˈ dlomwakǝn wai wa? <verse eid="JAS 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 2:5" />Kumini yelsǝni ini mudli nǝ mwani: Ase, Lya wolǝn miˈ lǝshi ulǝn kǝ dǝp lǝɓa sǝddǝm miˈ usǝn geˈ laˈti mbadlwaiya? si kǝ miˈ mbiˈ guˈ kǝ Lya nǝ pǝl dlǝlti tǝn ginǝ ɗǝ lyapti uwai ya? <verse eid="JAS 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 2:6" />Amma ki mbǝtl miˈgini bǝ ulǝn nisi ɗawai u. Ase, miˈusǝni ɗǝ mbitl kini waiwa? siɗǝ dǝtl kin twakina ɗǝ miˈpǝtl shilǝn waiwa? <verse eid="JAS 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 2:7" />Si ɗǝ dlǝb shilǝn kǝ kabbi tǝn shin mul naltu nǝ ɗǝ mbekkin nǝ nali uwai wa? <verse eid="JAS 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 2:8" />In ka shindǝlǝn ga tǝn kushti kǝ guˈ kǝ Lya u gunǝ geˈ shilǝn kǝ Lya kǝ laci u ɗǝ ussu, “lyam else dǝm twagi kǝnǝ gawagi,” ka pǝlin kǝ zokki i. <verse eid="JAS 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 2:9" />Amma in ka pǝlǝn lyab ga geˈ dlomwakǝn u, ka pǝlǝn bezǝn lǝɓa u ngu, tǝn kushti kǝ Musa ka dǝmni miˈ cetl zhili. <verse eid="JAS 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 2:10" />Amma mus mul nǝ ɗǝ katliˈ zhil kǝ Musa u, amma it cel gudǝl nǝmu, to mus ta cel zhilu ɓalu. <verse eid="JAS 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 2:11" />To ti u nǝˈ usu, “Bǝ pǝl kontwai u” Ti usu ɗaɗa nu, “Bǝ tlo mbalǝn wai.” To, in kapǝl kontwai u, amma iˈ tlo mbalǝn u, to, ka dǝm mul cetl zhilu ɓalu. <verse eid="JAS 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 2:12" />Gaki nǝgu, shilǝn wakǝn nǝ kyautǝn wakǝn tǝ dǝm kǝ miˈ ginǝ nǝn pǝlissi shilǝn kǝ zhil kǝ mbiˈ ga. <verse eid="JAS 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 2:13" />Amma gas pǝtl shilǝn Lya kǝn zǝˈ gontwai maˈmulnǝ bǝ ɗa zǝˈ gontwai u. Amma zǝˈ gonti nǝn ɗǝ tleˈ ga kǝ zǝˈ ɓatlti.<verse eid="JAS 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s">Laˈti mbadli Bǝ nǝ Kyautǝn kǝn wai u Use Kǝni</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 2:14" />Kini yelsǝni ini, ya kǝ mbuntwasi tǝ yakǝn mbalǝn usu laˈti mbatl nidɗa, bǝ kyautǝn was ɗawai u? anya, laˈti mbadlwasu nǝn pekkǝtl ti wa? <verse eid="JAS 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 2:15" />Cibǝlti, in yelsǝni mudli ko mwani, si dǝmti bǝ lulut nisi ɗawai u, hu anǝmi bǝ ulkǝ ɗami ɗa kǝpsiwai. <verse eid="JAS 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 2:16" />In gon wakǝn a ulsisu,“To, mbǝkǝcin swaca, tǝ Lya bǝlkin ulkǝ ɗami nǝ ulkǝ tle, nǝ ulkǝ laki” Bǝka bǝlǝnsi ulǝnwai u, mbuntwas nuna? <verse eid="JAS 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 2:17" />Nǝgu ɗa laˈti mbadli nǝm nǝ gwasi, bǝnǝ kyautǝn waswai u mǝcini. <verse eid="JAS 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 2:18" />Amma mulǝn nǝn ussu“ ai, kiɓo laˈti mbatl niˈ ɗa, ami ne ɓo sai kyautǝn.” To, mboki toh tǝn laˈti mbadlwagu, bǝ nǝ kyautǝn wai u, ami ne a mbokiˈ toh tǝn kyautǝn, yenti kǝ dwaɗǝn kǝ laˈti mbadli. <verse eid="JAS 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 2:19" />Ka ndǝgi Lya ɓo nǝm kǝma? A mbuni! to miˈgatl ma sa laˈmbatl nǝti i, amma hal si nepti kǝ dli nǝ ɓanti. <verse eid="JAS 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 2:20" />Ki mul lǝshi maˈ ulǝn! ko kǝnɗǝ lyamti hal nǝguni kiˈmani laˈti mbadli bǝ nǝ kyautǝn kǝn wai u, use kǝma? <verse eid="JAS 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="JAS 2:21" />Cin u nǝ bwasi nǝn Ablahim taˈ yakuwas Ishiyaku tǝn lu kyetl ulnǝ ɗǝ mbilliˈ Lya u, ashe gaki kyautǝn waskǝn manti ti mul zoˈ mbatl kǝn waiya? <verse eid="JAS 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="JAS 2:22" />Ka yeni laˈti mbadlwas ɗǝ lǝˈ neˈ kyautǝn wasi, kuma laˈti mbadwas a njikǝn tuˈ maˈ kyautǝn wasi. <verse eid="JAS 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="JAS 2:23" />I njikǝn shilǝn kǝ Lya nǝ usu,“Iblahim a laˈmbatl nǝ Lya i, laˈti mbadlwasu i ɓildli mbatl kǝ zokini maˈti,” I mbekki yelǝn ki Lya. <verse eid="JAS 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="JAS 2:24" />To ka yenini, Lya ɗǝ pekkǝtl yakǝn mbalǝn gaki kyautǝn wasi, bǝ gaki laˈti mbadlwas nǝmwai. <verse eid="JAS 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="JAS 2:25" />Gaki nǝgu Lahab mul pǝn neˈ mwani mbi peˈti gaki kyautǝn wa swaya? nǝn nje miˈshinkǝn i u, ippekkǝlsi tuˈtǝn shitu won. <verse eid="JAS 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="JAS 2:26" />Kǝnǝ kan unǝ dli ɗa bǝ lu shuˈti nidɗa wai u hwunini, nǝguma laˈti mbadli bǝnǝ kyautǝn wai u hwunini.<verse eid="JAS 2:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="JAS 3" />
  <para style="s">lǝga mul kon nǝ shilǝ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 3:1" />Kini yelsǝni ini, bǝ dǝmni kumwakǝn miˈkulciˈ mbalǝn wai, gaki manti wakǝn kǝni, mi miˈkulciˈ mbalǝn nǝn pǝlimmi shilǝn nǝ bǝna iye. <verse eid="JAS 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 3:2" />Gaki musinǝn mini miˈlwetini diɓǝli, in yakǝn mbalǝn ɗa dlǝb use geˈ shilǝn wa swai u, to muli kǝ njǝˈni tiɗa, tǝn maˈngapti mus kutlakǝn ki dli wasi. <verse eid="JAS 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 3:3" />Cibǝlti ngu, in a shimi bǝs ul kǝndǝ bi u gaki tǝˈ kumimi bi ɗani, nǝnǝgu mǝn maˈbǝlti nǝti mus lu u nǝmi lyamti u. <verse eid="JAS 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 3:4" />Nǝ yanǝn kundǝlǝn kǝ mal, ko nǝ si bazi u ndǝtl kǝ yetǝl ɗǝ jakǝˈsi, mus nǝnǝgu nǝ yakǝn domkǝn mul dǝlti ɗǝ gandǝtl ti mus lu u nǝ tin ngaki ɗa u. <verse eid="JAS 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 3:5" />Nǝ gu lǝga ma ɗa, tigu yakǝn ulǝn kǝni, sai bas laˈtibi! yanǝn kan unǝ yakǝn masɗi ɗǝ lakik bal dǝlgǝn utu u. <verse eid="JAS 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 3:6" />Lǝga ma utu ca! Ageˈ mus ku tlakǝn kǝ dli inǝn, lǝga tikǝ gǝskǝ bezǝn lǝɓa ti kon nǝ mus dli, mul hotti mbadli atliti, tine libi kǝ utu ɗǝ hottiti. <verse eid="JAS 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 3:7" />Yakǝn mbalǝn nǝn maˈ tlegga kǝ mus lǝɓa kǝ dǝlgǝn nǝkǝ ban, nǝkǝ geˈ mali nǝ yadli nǝ miˈ dǝtl tugi. <verse eid="JAS 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 3:8" />Amma yakǝn mbalǝn kǝn maˈ tlegga ki lǝga wai, ngashti ni gunǝ bǝkǝn maˈ dlǝtl ti wai u, kǝ njiˈni ɗa nǝ igǝn kǝ tloti. <verse eid="JAS 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 3:9" />Nǝ nali mi natl mul ban nǝ bwasi nǝn, nǝ nali mi byatl mbalǝn ginǝ pǝlsi geˈ teˈkǝ Lya u. <verse eid="JAS 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 3:10" />Nǝ bi nǝm kǝn ɗǝ natlti, nǝ byalti ɗaɗanu, yelsini ini, ai, gu a mbunwai! <verse eid="JAS 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 3:11" />Ko shu mal nǝm nǝn maˈ bǝtl mal mul tǝmtǝ, nǝ mal mul kukkudu ya? <verse eid="JAS 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 3:12" />Mil yelsini ini, pǝkkǝ ka nǝm maˈ utti mil kǝ zaitu ya? ko pǝkkǝ innabi nǝm maˈ zǝm mil kǝ ka ya? Tuˈ nǝgu shu mal mul bǝtl mal kǝ kukkudu kǝn bǝtl mal tǝmiwai.<verse eid="JAS 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="s">manti kǝ bali</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 3:13" />Mul manti nuna nǝ mul kal lǝɓa laplap a geˈ kini? An mboˈ tohtǝnki tuma zoˈdǝm twasi, nǝ kyautǝn kǝ zoki gunǝ ti pǝlti nǝ shindǝtl ga gunǝ ɗǝ peˈti geˈ ma' ulǝn u. <verse eid="JAS 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 3:14" />Amma in bezǝn nget mbalǝn nikin ɗa nǝ lyap ga u ageˈ mbadlwakǝn u, bǝˈpǝn ɓulmǝn nǝ nǝ guwai, aki nget baliwai. <verse eid="JAS 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 3:15" />Undi manti gu sul lya kǝn ɗǝ ndassuɗwai kǝ dǝp lǝɓani, kǝ lyap mbatl kǝni kǝ sheɗan. <verse eid="JAS 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 3:16" />mus geˈlu unǝ nget ɗa nǝ lyap ga u, alǝbi dlati nǝ mus bezǝn lǝɓa ma ɗa. <verse eid="JAS 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 3:17" />Amma manti kǝ sul lya u, kǝ kina kǝ zokini, mul shindǝtl ga kǝni, mul natl kǝ ga kǝn wai, mul zoˈ mbadli, mul lyap dǝb kǝ zoki, alhelini, mul zoˈ mbadli mul bi nǝm, mul pǝtl bali, mul nǝ bǝ ɗa wotl mbalǝn wai u. <verse eid="JAS 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 3:18" />Undi mutti kǝ mbadli gunǝ u miˈ bwasti dlati ɗǝ watlti u, i mbǝtl zoˈ mbadli.<verse eid="JAS 3:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="JAS 4" />
  <para style="s">Pǝtl Yelǝn nǝ dǝp lǝɓa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 4:1" />Yakǝn ɗǝ mbǝtl ngeˈ elsǝni nǝ dlati a geˈ dlomwakǝn? ase, bǝ lyap lǝɓa hukkǝn ɗǝ latikin ɗǝ dlan nǝ yelsǝni ambadwakǝn wai ya? <verse eid="JAS 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 4:2" />Kǝn lyap lǝɓa aˈ hwolini, aˈtlo mbalǝn. kǝn lyap lǝɓa, bǝ kǝkkǝn mbitini wai, aˈ tlilǝn dlati. Ki hwoltini gaki ki ɗa shilǝn nǝ Lya wai kǝni. <verse eid="JAS 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 4:3" />Kǝn shilǝnti nǝ Lya aˈ hwolini, gaki ki nǝ bezǝn mbatl kǝn ki pǝlini, gaki ki konni nǝ nali tǝn kup tǝp kǝ gawakǝn. <verse eid="JAS 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 4:4" />Kini miˈ lǝshi zoˈmbadli! Ki manini yelǝn nǝ dǝp lǝɓa ngel Lya kǝn waiya? gaki nǝgu, mus mulnǝ ɗǝ lyap pǝtl yelǝn nǝ dǝp lǝɓa u, ta pal gawas mul ngel lya u ngu. <verse eid="JAS 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 4:5" />Kin nǝ yentini tǝn swi kǝn shilǝn kǝ Lya usu, “Yal kǝ mbatl kǝ Lya gunǝ Lya shimi geˈ mini u nǝn ɗǝ mbuttimi iye ya? <verse eid="JAS 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 4:6" />Amma ti bǝtl min alheli diɓǝli. I laki ɗa shilǝn kǝ Lya usu: “Lya ɗǝ ngeˈmiˈnatl kǝ ga, amma ti pǝliˈmiˈshindǝtl ga alheli.” <verse eid="JAS 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 4:7" />Gaki nǝgu takkǝn gawakǝn maˈLya, aˈnge lǝɓa kǝ shedan, ti kuma tǝn kitǝlliˈkini. <verse eid="JAS 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 4:8" />Shaˈni maˈLya tima tǝn shaˈti makini. Dǝmni nǝ mbatl kǝ zokki, kini miˈbezǝn mbadli, wokǝlǝn mbadlwakǝn taka, kini miˈmbatl lop. <verse eid="JAS 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 4:9" />Pǝlǝn du mbadli, kulni, pǝlǝn lu. hwe tǝ getltwakǝn pal kulu, hwol tuggwakǝn tǝpal du mbadli. <verse eid="JAS 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 4:10" />Shindǝlǝn gawakǝn maˈmulban, tima tǝn natl kini.<verse eid="JAS 4:10" /></para>
  <para style="s">Bǝˈzi yelse kapbi wai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 4:11" />Kini mil yesǝni ini, bǝˈbyalǝn yelsǝni wai. Gaki ko wokǝn byal yelse wasi mul bǝlti, ko mul nǝ a zi yelse was kapbi u, ta byal pǝtl shilǝn u ɓalu, ta ziˈkapbi u ngu. In ka zi pǝtl shilǝn kapbi u, ki mul bitl tiwai, ki mul zitti kapbi ni. <verse eid="JAS 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 4:12" />Mul bǝtl shilǝn nǝm kǝni, tikǝ mul pǝtl ti, tikǝ mul ndǝltl kǝ pekkǝlti nǝ mǝcǝlti. to, kikǝ wongi kiˈzi yelke waˈkapbi?<verse eid="JAS 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="s">Bǝˈpǝl laˈti bi gaki kyau wai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 4:13" />Gakǝn kǝm, kini u nǝ ɗǝ usu,“Asǝti ko akyau mǝn lǝti geˈgatl gwaˈ, an pǝl hwon tyaka, ami ulti nǝ ulti taka am mbi ulpi.” <verse eid="JAS 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 4:14" />I ngu kǝ manǝn ulnǝ tǝ nda kyau uwai. Undǝ dli ukǝn nikini? ai, kǝnǝ wolkǝndǝ ɗa, alǝm dǝmtu nǝn gǝlti. <verse eid="JAS 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 4:15" />Mbun ni kǝ ulnisu,“ In Lya a ndǝgu, in mi geˈmiˈdli u, mǝn pǝtl gu nǝ gu.” <verse eid="JAS 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 4:16" />Amma i ngu, nǝguni ki laˈtibi nǝ dun ngesi. Undǝ laˈtibi gu bezǝn ulǝn kǝnǝ. <verse eid="JAS 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 4:17" />Gaki nǝgu, mus mulnǝ a man zoˈlǝɓa u, in nge pǝlti u, ta pǝl bezǝn lǝɓa u ngu.<verse eid="JAS 4:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="JAS 5" />
  <para style="s">Dǝliˈ miˈ Usǝn Kǝm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="JAS 5:1" />To kumini kini miˈ usǝn! Kulni nǝ laˈti yali gaki bǝna u nǝtǝ mbǝtǝn kini u. <verse eid="JAS 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="JAS 5:2" />Usǝn wakǝn mus ɓosini, luˈlǝgǝllwakǝn mus shisshil a ɗam i. <verse eid="JAS 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="JAS 5:3" />Zinaliya nǝ azulpa wakǝn sa koni, kontwasǝn u nǝn dǝmti yenti kǝ dwaɗǝn tǝn kini, kǝn ɗap tlu kǝ dli ɗakini kǝnǝ utu. Ka domi gawakǝn usǝn i ageˈ paˈti kǝ ndallǝɓa i. <verse eid="JAS 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="JAS 5:4" />Yanini! upkǝ miˈkyautǝn u nǝˈ nge ɓatl tisi u si kulu maˈ Lya. Kulu kǝ miˈ otlikin lǝɓa taka a mbǝkǝci kǝm ɗǝˈ “Lya mul nalti i. <verse eid="JAS 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="JAS 5:5" />Ka pǝlǝn dǝp lǝɓa i geˈ tǝmti, ki ɗamti nǝ tleti nǝ kon nǝ lǝɓa. To, ka katlǝn gawakǝn i gaki cin kǝ poshti. <verse eid="JAS 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="JAS 5:6" />Ka poci mul zoˈmbatl ɓatlti, kuma tloti, bǝ ta lwe mbatl nǝ kini wai.<verse eid="JAS 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="s">Ngashti bi ageˈ Bǝna</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="JAS 5:7" />Gaki nǝgu mil yelsǝni, ngacem bi, hal gas patl kǝ mulban. Yanǝn kan unǝ mul kotl lu ɗǝ ngashti bi ɗǝ ɓutti cin unǝ tǝ guwas bǝl gwe kǝ zoki u.Nǝ ngashti bi iye ti ɓutti mal kǝ otlti o nǝ mal kǝ gisi. <verse eid="JAS 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="JAS 5:8" />Aˈdǝmni nǝ ngashti bi. Aˈ dlǝllǝn mbadlwakǝn, gaki mbǝˈ kǝ mulban ɓal nja i. <verse eid="JAS 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="JAS 5:9" />Yelsǝni bǝ nalǝn ni tǝn yelsǝni wai, gaki ɓa zikin ɓatlti, i ngu mul pǝtl shilǝn ɓaltǝn bidlabi i! <verse eid="JAS 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="JAS 5:10" />Tǝn cimbǝlti nǝ ngashtibi geˈ bǝna, yelsǝni, yanǝn miˈnjeˈshinkǝn ki Lya ma nǝs shilǝn nǝ shin kǝ mulban u. <verse eid="JAS 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="JAS 5:11" />I ngu, mǝnɗǝ ndwaˈti ginǝ ngashbi i, ka kumǝn un ndi ngashtibi unǝ Ayuba pǝli u, ka yenǝn un ndi paˈti bisi u nǝ “Lya kǝ njiˈni, nǝ kup ciˈgonti, mul zǝˈgonti. <verse eid="JAS 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="JAS 5:12" />Amma tǝn ko yan ngi, yelsǝni, bǝˈ lenceniwai, ko nǝ lya, ko nǝ atli, ko mus undi lenceti ukǝni. Ənka ulnisu “E u,” A dǝm tǝn “E” katl, ǝn ka ulnisu “Oˈ o”, A dliltǝn “Oˈ o” i katl, gaki in nǝgu wai u nǝn zikin ɓatlti. <verse eid="JAS 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="JAS 5:13" />Ən gon wakǝn ɗǝ tleˈ bǝna u, to, aˈ shilǝn nǝ “Lya, ǝn gon wakǝn ɗǝ kup hwol tuga? To, aˈul wul kǝ dwati “Lya. <verse eid="JAS 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="JAS 5:14" />Ko gon wakǝn nǝn ɗǝ gonti? To, am mbe kolsi kǝ Ikilisiya bi as ngemiˈ “Lya, asi swatitti mil nǝ shin kǝ mul ban. <verse eid="JAS 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="JAS 5:15" />Ngep Lya ki laˈti mbadli, nǝn ndokǝtl mul gonti Lya nǝn tlilti lya, in ma tapǝl bezǝn lǝɓa u, nǝn pecitti. <verse eid="JAS 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="JAS 5:16" />Gaki nǝgu, aˈgopǝn dlimiˈ yelsǝni bezǝn lǝɓa wakǝn, a ki ngemi yelkǝni Lya, gaki kiˈ mbi doˈti ɗa. Shilǝn nǝ Lya kǝ mul zoˈmbadli kyautǝnwas ndǝlni iye. <verse eid="JAS 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="JAS 5:17" />Iliya yakǝn mbalǝn kǝni kǝnǝ mini, amma nǝˈ gob ngep Lya u gaki bǝ mal mbǝwai u, sai nǝpǝl hwon maki nǝ li mǝkka bǝ mal a mbǝ geˈ atliwai. <verse eid="JAS 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="JAS 5:18" />Kal ki nǝgu nǝn ngem Lya ɗaɗanu u, i mal mbǝ sul lya, atl ne ibbǝl gwei lǝɓa wasi. <verse eid="JAS 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="JAS 5:19" />Yelsǝni ini, in gon wakǝn a zaˈshitu kǝ Lya u, a gon wakǝn palti teˈtǝn shitu. <verse eid="JAS 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="JAS 5:20" />Am maninca mus mulnǝ a pal mul pǝtl bezǝn lǝɓa teˈtǝn shitu u ta pekkǝl mul bezǝn lǝɓa i ɗǝgeˈ mǝshti, gu nǝn dǝmti shitu kǝ peshti lipǝn diɓǝli.<verse eid="JAS 5:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="JAS 5" />
</usx>